      "title": "HTTP/DoH: Adjust the expected base64url length for no padding",
      "message": "HTTP/DoH: Adjust the expected base64url length for no padding\n\nAdjust the expected length after base64url decoding when DoH is\npresent for how padding characters MUST NOT be used.\n\nAlso, add a comment about how stream IDs are not retrieved yet\nfor HTTP/3 (#21388)\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2026-07-04T00:27:05.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2026-07-04T07:50:17.000-04:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/d9c3518efb4aaa5eb03b94bec9344364a61bd066"
    },
    {
      "id": "9a4e9a70451263a0482430067f9b29a96ad0062b",
      "short_id": "9a4e9a70",
      "created_at": "2026-07-04T07:50:13.000-04:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "f2dd5a68b134239a0c6876a31d286c7314ac27e0"
      ],
      "title": "epan: Handle base64url encoding padding being optional",
      "message": "epan: Handle base64url encoding padding being optional\n\nUnlike the standard base64 encoding, in base64url encoding padding\nwith '=' is optional:\n\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc4648/#section-5\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc4648/#section-3.2\n\nAnd in certain uses, like DNS over HTTP, padding MUST NOT be\nincluded:\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8484/#section-6\n\nHandle that in our base64url decoding function.\n\nPing #21384\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2026-07-04T00:24:12.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
